.TH HULL 1 "2026-11-26" "hull 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hull \- run one machine spec as a container, a virtual machine or an emulation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hull plan
.RB [ \-f
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-backend
.IR B ]
.RB [ \-\-explain ]
.RB [ \-\-resolved ]
.br
.B hull run
.RB [ \-f
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-backend
.IR B ]
.RI [ NAME ]
.br
.B hull exec
.RB [ \-t ]
.I ID
.B \-\-
.IR COMMAND ...
.br
.B hull stop
.I ID
.br
.B hull ps
.br
.B hull import \-\-machine
.I X.vbox|X.vmx|X.ovf|X.ova DIR
.br
.B hull doctor
.br
.B hull \-\-help
|
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hull
reads a machine from
.IR hull.conf ,
a plain file beside the directory it runs, and runs it on the engine its
.B (backend ...)
names: in user namespaces
.RB ( chroot ),
under KVM
.RB ( vm ),
in full software emulation
.RB ( emu ),
under Docker, VirtualBox, or as a whole PC or microcontroller board of its
own
.RB ( pc ).
Changing that one line moves the same files from one to another.
Nothing runs as root: the resident part is a per-user core, started when
needed and gone when idle.
.PP
.B hull plan
says what each engine does with every field of the spec \(em native,
emulated, or refused \(em before anything runs.
.B hull run
starts the machine, its output on stdout and its exit status the
command's.
.B hull exec \-t ID \-\- console
joins a terminal to a pc or board machine's serial port;
.B console 2
is a board's second UART.
.PP
VirtualBox and VMware machines and appliances run from their own files
.RB ( "hull run \-f Old.vbox" ),
or are copied into a folder of hull's own by
.BR "hull import \-\-machine" ,
their disks converted to qcow2.
.PP
.B hull \-\-help
lists every command.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I hull.conf
the machine, read from the current directory unless
.B \-f
names another.
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/hull/
hull itself and what it reads beside itself: the guest agents, and hull's
own kernel where it was built.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/hull/
the core's socket and the running machines.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/hull/
the optional image store.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hull-gui (1),
.BR qemu (1)
